{
"opening": "The boltons library is releasing updates that affect core utility classes and string handling functions, which are dependencies for the glom project. To ensure compatibility and access to new features, glom must integrate these specific changes from the updated boltons release. The following requirements define the observable public API behaviors that must be present in both projects.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m08",
"text": "In boltons, the OneToOne class must correctly handle inputs where values are not unique by maintaining insertion order and allowing multiple keys to map to the same value without raising errors. The FastIterOrderedMultiDict and unique utilities must support this non-unique one-to-one mapping behavior as documented."
},
{
"id": "m12",
"text": "In boltons, the FunctionBuilder.get_defaults_dict method must include keyword-only argument defaults in its returned dictionary. The formatargandannotation function and inspect_formatargspec must provide consistent formatting for function arguments without triggering Python 3 warnings."
},
{
"id": "m12c",
"text": "In boltons, observed through glom's usage, the FunctionBuilder.get_defaults_dict method must include keyword-only argument defaults in its returned dictionary. The formatargandannotation function and inspect_formatargspec must provide consistent formatting for function arguments without triggering Python 3 warnings."
},
{
"id": "m19",
"text": "In boltons, the difference_update method on set-like objects must support reverse subtraction via __rsub__, allowing operations like set() - custom_set to work correctly when the left operand does not support intersection with the right operand's type."
},
{
"id": "m22",
"text": "In glom, the glom and glomit functions must correctly process specifications involving Auto, Check, Fill, First, Inspect, Iter, Let, and other spec types without raising GlomError during conflict resolution scenarios. The chunked, dropwhile, filter, first, flatten, and all utilities must maintain their standard iteration and transformation behaviors as defined in the public API."
}
],
"closing": "Please verify that these behaviors are implemented and exposed correctly in the respective projects before proceeding with the release integration."
}
